          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Verona and the Italian Setting",
          "content": "Shakespeare's Verona is half real, half imagined. The northern Italian city-states of the late medieval and early Renaissance period were notorious for feuds among aristocratic clans. The Montecchi and Cappelletti were actual Veronese families mentioned by Dante (Purgatorio VI). For Elizabethan audiences, Italy connoted passion, intrigue, Catholicism, and exotic danger.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Verona</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A City of Stones and Grudges</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"180\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Historical Setting</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"260\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Northern Italy, 14th-15th century</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">An independent city-state under Prince Escalus</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"330\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Real Montecchi clan banished from Verona, 1324</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"420\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Elizabethan View of Italy</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"465\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Land of poets (Petrarch, Dante, Boccaccio)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Land of vendetta, poison, and intrigue</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Catholic: friars, confessionals, sacraments</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"600\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"640\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Setting Resonances</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"685\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sun-baked piazzas: heat breeds quarrels (I.i, III.i)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walled gardens: forbidden meetings (II.ii)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The tomb: ancestral honor and death (V.iii)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shakespeare never visited Italy</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\">His Verona is the Verona of imagination</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Place as moral and emotional climate</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Italy in the English imagination: a hotter, more passionate, more dangerous world."
          }
